#X text 240 83 the object records incoming messages and plays them
back with the original timing;
#X text 240 123 recording and playback are controlled by the [rec(
\, [play( \, [stop( \, [clear( and [flush( messages;
#X text 240 163 @auto starts recording on the first input atom \, @r
sets the number of repeats \, @speed sets the playback speed;
#X text 240 203 @sync uses an external bang pulse to synchronize the
recorded events;
#X text 240 243 the object can be used to record a live performance
gesture and loop it \, for example to record a short keyboard phrase
and play it back in a loop;
